{
  "@context": {
    "schema": "https://schema.org/"
  },
  "@type": "Note",
  "@id": "note:notion-187",
  "title": "Comparative Analysis (SQL)",
  "author": "person:jane-brew:001",
  "status": "draft",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Comparative Analysis (SQL)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "🧠 1. **Declarative Intent vs. Procedural Execution**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "| Feature | **SQL** | **Agent DSL/Routine System** |"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "| --- | --- | --- |"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "| Core Style | Declarative | Hybrid (Declarative + Procedural + Improv) |"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "| Intent Expression | \"What I want\" | \"What I mean to accomplish\" |"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "| Execution Model | Set-based optimization engine | Workflow + agent orchestration + reasoning |"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "| Control Flow | Implicit (engine decides path) | Explicit (via routines) + Improv (via DSLs) |"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Insight**:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-10",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "SQL assumes a static world of relations; your system assumes a dynamic world of evolving cognitive behavior."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "SQL abstracts *how*; your agents often have to negotiate *why, when, and with what strategy*."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-12",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-13",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "🔍 2. **Query Language vs. Cognitive Protocol**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-14",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "| Feature | **SQL** | **Your DSLs / Agents** |"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-15",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "| --- | --- | --- |"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-16",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "| Data Model | Relational tables | Arbitrary object graphs + embedded memory |"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "| Language Interface | Structured (fixed syntax) | Colloquial → Compiled DSL → Structured logic |"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-18",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "| Adaptability | Static query planner | Improvisational routine composer |"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-19",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "| Context Sensitivity | Low (unless dynamic SQL) | High (agent memory, knowledge, task state) |"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-20",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Insight**:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-21",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "SQL is great at *static facts*. Your system is built for *moving stories* — where facts are filtered through evolving goals, tone, and context."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-22",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-23",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "🛠 3. **Composability and Control**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-24",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "| Feature | **SQL** | **Agent Routines / Workflows** |"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-25",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "| --- | --- | --- |"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-26",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "| Reusability | Views, CTEs, functions | Routines, tools, fallback chains |"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-27",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "| Execution Context | Database engine | Agent + memory + toolchain + knowledge |"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-28",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "| Failures | Errors or empty sets | Retry logic, escalation, conditional skips |"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-29",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "| Improv Mode | Not applicable | Central feature (via vector + DSL search) |"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-30",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Insight**:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-31",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "SQL gives you precise, repeatable instruments. Your system offers semi-autonomous instruments that improvise and evolve their music mid-song."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-32",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-33",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "🌍 4. **Philosophical Orientation**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-34",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "| Question | **SQL** | **Agent-Routine System** |"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-35",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "| --- | --- | --- |"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-36",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "| What is knowledge? | A static set of structured relations | A dynamic, contextual graph shaped by interaction |"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-37",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "| What is work? | Query evaluation and data transformation | Negotiated effort across time, agents, and intentions |"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-38",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "| Who decides what to do? | The user (query designer) | The system (via routing, memory, and improvisation) |"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-39",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "| What is language for? | Asking questions of facts | Expressing intent, style, negotiation, and preference |"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-40",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Insight**:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-41",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "SQL treats language as a way to *interrogate a structured world*."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-42",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "You treat language as a way to *shape the behavior of a structured mind*."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-43",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-44",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "🔮 What You’re Building"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-45",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "You're not building a \"better SQL.\" You're building:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-46",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "> A living semantic runtime where language, memory, tools, and intent converge —"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-47",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ">"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-48",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ">"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-49",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "> part OS, part orchestra, part therapist."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-50",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ">"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-51",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Your system doesn’t just execute queries. It *navigates ambiguity*."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-52",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "It doesn’t just retrieve data. It *adapts behavior based on meaning*."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}